diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 79c75b0..c3687df 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -292,6 +292,80 @@ Rate limiting is a per-address token bucket: `CommandsPerMinute` is the sustaine
 inside `FailWindowSeconds` refuse that address for `BanSeconds`, enforced at `accept`
 before the password is read.
 
+## Tick metrics
+
+`GET /api/metrics` uses the existing REST bearer-token and IP access controls and
+returns HTTP 200 for metric availability states. Example values below are synthetic:
+
+```json
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "tick": {
+    "status": "ready",
+    "source": "engine_tick_hook",
+    "scope": "UDomGameEngine::Tick",
+    "reason": "",
+    "windowSeconds": 1,
+    "sampleCount": 5,
+    "lastSampleAgeSeconds": 0.25,
+    "observedAtUnixMs": 1800000001000,
+    "rateHz": 5,
+    "executionMs": {"p50": 3, "p95": 100, "p99": 100}
+  }
+}
+```
+
+All numeric fields inside `tick` are null unless `status` is `ready`.
+Other statuses are `starting`, `warming`, `unsupported`, `stale`, `faulted`, and
+`stopped`; `reason` explains the state. Engine readiness gates publication only.
+The producer installs synchronously in the preload constructor before the API's
+initialization thread, without waiting for players, RPCs, or API requests.
+
+Execution means monotonic elapsed wall time inside the entire original
+`UDomGameEngine::Tick` invocation. This includes its pre/post delegates and nested
+base/world work, including normal return through a tail call. It excludes work
+outside this call in FEngineLoop and asynchronous work that outlives its return.
+The original receives unchanged arguments exactly once, even when sampling stops.
+
+Select completed ticks from a ten-second lookback, keeping the immediately
+preceding completion as the anchor. During startup the first completion becomes
+the anchor. With N subsequent records, cadence is N divided by the elapsed time
+between anchor and last completion. `windowSeconds` reports that actual interval,
+which can exceed ten seconds after a long tick. At least one second of coverage
+and one record after the anchor are required. Percentiles use exactly those N
+durations and the nearest-rank definition. A freshly completed long tick is
+included even if it began before the lookback. There is no clipping or sampling
+of only the most recently visible engine timing scalar.
+
+Storage is 8,192 records plus an eviction anchor. Eviction of still-needed records
+makes metrics unavailable until a complete window can be formed; ordinary wrap
+of old records is harmless. More than two seconds without a completion is stale.
+An in-flight tick has no known complete duration. `observedAtUnixMs` is Unix epoch
+milliseconds captured for the latest completed sample, not the HTTP response
+time. `lastSampleAgeSeconds` uses the monotonic clock. C2 should preserve nulls,
+use observation time for freshness, and never average percentiles across windows.
+
+The only supported profile is x86-64 ET_EXEC build ID `c695030ea461f775`, with
+zero load bias. The actual dedicated object uses `_ZTV14UDomGameEngine` at
+`0x2252888`, address point `0x2252898`. Slot 98 at `0x2252ba8` must contain
+`0x9d30db0`. Installation validates the full build ID, mapped ELF headers, exact
+entry/dispatch/base-call/world-call/return bytes, private page permissions, and
+that GEngine at `0xdfc1b70` is still null. An executable preinit array is rejected.
+The first and subsequent samples corroborate the object against GEngine and the
+expected vptr. Unknown builds fail closed. There is no late installation retry.
+
+Both build systems link the library with `-z nodelete` so the forwarding code and
+process-lifetime state survive while the slot references them. Stop disables
+sampling and does not unpatch. Failure to restore page permissions leaves valid
+forwarding but faults metrics and fails runtime acceptance. No game file is
+modified by this producer.
+
+Run `make -j1 test` for native arithmetic, overflow/recovery, forwarding/unwind,
+unknown-build rejection, concurrency and response-schema checks. These tests do
+not start the game or validate the actual binary's runtime behavior. Packaging,
+empty-server verification, overhead measurement and C2 integration remain part
+of the parent-controlled actualgameverification workflow.
+
 ## SDK
 
 The engine layer is driven by a Dumper-7 dump of the server binary, which is not included
